---
import { site } from '../config';
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Contact"
  eyebrow="Contact and support"
  description="How to contact the people responsible for torwache, report bugs, and handle private or security-sensitive information."
>
  <h1>Contact</h1>

  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.contacts.general}`}>{site.contacts.general}</a> when a question
    needs a private reply from the company responsible for torwache. Use{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contacts.privacy}`}>{site.contacts.privacy}</a> for privacy requests.
    Messages are handled by {site.legal.operatorName} in Berlin, Germany. There is no outsourced
    support desk and no user account to look up.
  </p>

  <h2>Bug reports and feature requests</h2>
  <p>
    Reproducible bugs and public feature discussions belong in the{' '}
    <a href={site.issuesUrl}>GitHub issue tracker</a>. Include the torwache version, Chrome version,
    operating system, the steps that caused the problem, and what you expected to happen. Before
    opening a new report, check whether an existing issue already covers it. Do not paste private
    browsing information, credentials, or personal data into a public issue.
  </p>

  <h2>Security-sensitive reports</h2>
  <p>
    Send suspected vulnerabilities to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contacts.security}`}>{site.contacts.security}</a> rather than publishing
    exploit details in the issue tracker. Describe the affected version, the impact, and the
    smallest reliable way to reproduce the problem. Avoid sending real credentials or unrelated
    browsing data. Receipt can be acknowledged, but torwache is free software and does not offer a
    contractual response or remediation time.
  </p>

  <h2>Before writing</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/guides/">guides</a> cover installation, permissions, local storage, and blocker
    selection. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains which information the extension
    and website handle. The <a href={site.repositoryUrl}>source repository</a> contains the licence,
    release history, tests, and implementation. torwache has no account recovery, billing, or
    subscription support because it has no accounts, billing, or subscriptions.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
